  "content": {
    "introduction": "This evidence matrix compiles treatment efficacy data from the highest-quality systematic reviews and clinical guidelines. Evidence levels follow standard grading: A (multiple RCTs or meta-analyses), B (single RCT or large observational studies), C (case series or expert consensus), D (case reports or theoretical basis only). NNT (number needed to treat) represents how many patients need to receive treatment for one additional patient to benefit compared to placebo.",
    "disclaimer": "This matrix is for educational purposes only. Treatment decisions should be made with a qualified healthcare provider based on individual patient factors, preferences, and circumstances. Evidence levels may change as new research emerges."
  },
